      "Unattended scheduled routine, branch claude/upbeat-dijkstra-dkntmy, picked up at origin/main tip b6d946e3 (PR #701, merging post-700-tiers-2-5-research-agent-reconfirmed-clean) — HEAD matched origin/main exactly at session start. Confirmed baseline green: npm ci (409 packages, 0 vulnerabilities), npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors), npm run lint (clean), npx vitest run (2827 passed, 201 files — matching the prior iteration's own reported count exactly). mcp__github__list_pull_requests reconfirmed the sole open PR is still #202 (unrelated, weeks-stale human draft). Full `git fetch origin '+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*' --prune` (629 remote heads) plus a committer-date sweep of the newest ~24 claude/* branches (all ahead=0 or carrying only already-merged commits under a different SHA) confirmed no live fold candidate. The empty-backlog diff-gate against the documented anchor (a5c25e04) showed exactly one commit since (ee1350c1, the prior iteration's own tiers-2-5-reconfirmed-clean entry, itself only touching the two process-log files) — a sixth consecutive zero-product-diff window, so per the waste-reduction rule this skipped a from-scratch tiered sweep and went straight to the tier-6/8 candidates the prior iteration's AGENT_PROTOCOL note pointed at (accessibility, LLM prompt-injection surface, Stripe Connect onboarding-link expiry/retry handling).",
    rationale:
      "Own read of the LLM prompt-injection surface (src/lib/marketing/generators.ts's AnthropicMarketingGenerator, src/lib/marketing/deliver-pack.ts, src/lib/voice/deliver-pack.ts) came back genuinely clean: model output is strictly parsed (parseVariantsJson extracts the JSON array, validates length against the server-controlled contentTypes array — never model-controlled — and rejects on any mismatch), every title/body/cta/hashtags field is escaped via escapeHtmlForEmail/plainTextToEmailHtml before landing in an outbound email, dashboard rendering uses plain JSX text nodes (no dangerouslySetInnerHTML), and Buffer posts go out as a plain-text form field, never interpreted as markup — so even a maximally adversarial businessName/services/tagline (the only lead-supplied fields that reach the prompt) can only distort that same lead's own generated content, never escape into HTML/script/SSRF, and never cross into a different lead's data. Investigating the Stripe Connect payout scaffold's onboarding-link handling (src/lib/commerce/stripe-connect.ts, createStripeConnectOnboardingLinkAction in src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts) found a real, live gap: Stripe's account_onboarding Account Links are single-use and expire quickly if not opened, but the only existing dashboard flow (handleGetStripeConnectOnboardingLink in leads-client.tsx) copied the freshly-minted URL to the operator's clipboard with an alert saying 'copied — send it to the client' — a manual copy, switch to an email/text client, paste, and send that routinely takes longer than the link's live window, handing the client an already-dead URL with no indication anything had expired. Shipped a second path that closes this race structurally instead of just warning about it: sendStripeConnectOnboardingLinkEmail (src/lib/email/resend.ts, skipSuppression: true — same billing-critical class as the dunning/subscription-pause notices, not cold marketing) and sendStripeConnectOnboardingLinkToClientAction (src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts, mirrors createStripeConnectOnboardingLinkAction's auth/rate-limit/gate/existence-check chain, adds a lead.email presence check, and always mints a brand-new link via createConnectOnboardingLink rather than reusing/caching one — so a second click after an expired first attempt just works) generate and deliver the link to the client's inbox in the same server request, eliminating the manual hand-off delay entirely. Wired a new 'Email onboarding link' button into leads-client.tsx next to the existing 'Get onboarding link' (copy) button — kept the copy path too (an operator may want to hand-deliver via phone/text instead) but updated its alert copy to state the link is single-use and expires within minutes and to point at the new email button as the more reliable default. Did not build a persisted expiry countdown, auto-resend-on-expiry, or a durable 'link sent' marker — this is a dormant, ALLOW_STRIPE_CONNECT_ONBOARDING-gated scaffold with no live traffic yet (commerce-payouts-stripe-connect itself stays operator/legal-gated pending counsel review of the money-movement half), and per AGENT_PROTOCOL's anti-scope-creep guidance a single focused fix (closing the actual expiry race for the one delivery path that exists) is the right size for this iteration; a resend/expiry-tracking UI can be a follow-up once real onboarding volume exists to justify it. Tests: 4 new cases in stripe-connect-actions.test.ts (no-account error, no-email error, success path asserting createConnectOnboardingLink is called then sendStripeConnectOnboardingLinkEmail with the exact minted URL, and a send-failure passthrough) and 2 new cases in resend.test.ts (skipSuppression bypass, href-escaping of an adversarial onboardingUrl). Verified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors), npm run lint (clean), npx vitest run (2833 passed, up from 2827 — 6 new, 201 files, no new file), a full clean rebuild (rm -rf .next && npm run build, clean, same 42-route ○/ƒ split), and an npm run dev sanity check with ALLOW_STRIPE_CONNECT_ONBOARDING=1 (/dashboard/leads 200; the new button sits inside the per-lead Commerce-catalog-editor panel, which only renders once an operator opens that editor for a paid/commerceAddon-eligible lead — the seeded demo leads don't reach that state, so the button wasn't reachable via a plain page-load curl, but the surrounding JSX/handler wiring is byte-identical in structure to the already-working 'Get onboarding link' button it sits beside; dev server killed, port 3000 confirmed freed). NEXT_STEPS unchanged — all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked; this is a hardening fix on an already-shipped dormant scaffold, not a resolution of any gated item. Diff-gate anchor moves to b6d946e3 (this iteration's own starting tip).",
